.IX Title "Lucy::Store::FSFolder 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Store::FSFolder 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Store::FSFolder \- File System implementation of Folder.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 3
\&    my $folder = Lucy::Store::FSFolder\->new(
\&        path => \*(Aq/path/to/folder\*(Aq,
\&    );
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Implementation of Folder using a single file system
directory and multiple files.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 3
\&    my $folder = Lucy::Store::FSFolder\->new(
\&        path => \*(Aq/path/to/folder\*(Aq,
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new Folder.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBpath\fR \- Location of the index. If the specified directory does
not exist already, it will NOT be created, in order to prevent
misconfigured read applications from spawning bogus files – so it may
be necessary to create the directory yourself.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Store::FSFolder isa Lucy::Store::Folder isa Clownfish::Obj.
